Package: assignmentB2MadelineWoodley
Title: Calculate Grouped Means
Version: 1.0.0
Authors@R: 
    person("Madeline", "Woodley", email = "madeline.woodley@ubc.ca", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: This package contains a single function, `groupedmeans()`, which allows users to efficiently group information within their dataframe, `data`, based on values in a variable, `var1` (usually categorical), within their dataset and calculate the mean of values for another (numeric) variable, `var2`, in their dataset based on the `var1` groupings. The function returns a summary table with `var1` and the associated grouped `var2` means. Note that the function is written to retain missing (NA) values for `var2`.
